# Dev team orchestration

## Gate: explicit `/dev-team` only

- **Start the multi-role team pipeline only when the *current* user message contains the exact command `/dev-team`** (optionally with a task description after it).
- Do **not** assemble the cast, launch BA/PM/orchestrator pipeline, or spawn role subagents because of soft phrasing («собери команду», «команда», «feature team», «dev-team», «оркестрируй») without `/dev-team`.
- Without `/dev-team`: work as a **normal single agent** (implement / fix / explore yourself). You may honor a **single** explicit role slash like `/backend-dev` / `/qa` if the user typed that. Do **not** invent a full team, bug fast-path cast, or epic+AC pipeline.
- **Hard ban — `Task(subagent_type: "orchestrator")`:** never call it unless the *current* user message contains `/dev-team`, or you are **resuming the same** `/dev-team` stage (user «ок» / «делай» / grill answers for that already-open cast). A prior turn that once used orchestrator does **not** authorize later unrelated asks.
- When the gate is open and you spawn orchestrator, the Task prompt **must** include the exact line `dev_team_authorized: true` (and preferably quote the user `/dev-team` line). Without that marker, orchestrator must refuse.
- Continuations resume **that** cast only — do **not** start a **new** team/slug from soft phrasing alone.

Parent Agent acts as the **orchestrator** (see also `.cursor/agents/orchestrator.md`) **only inside an active `/dev-team` run**. Prefer custom subagents in `.cursor/agents/` for role-shaped work when the gate is open. Do not invent parallel process that skips `task-intake.mdc` / grill / specs / user «ок» before production code.

## Role cast (PM owns staffing)

- **Roster** = catalog of available roles (table below). Not every ticket runs every role.
- **PM** publishes an ordered **role cast** in `agent.md` + the pm issue handoff: who is in, who is out, parallel marks (`∥`), eng/packages owners.
- **Orchestrator launches only roles in the cast**, in cast order. Do **not** invent or “add for safety” roles outside the cast (except an explicit **user** override that updates the cast).
- Heuristics for when to staff architect / security / tech-writer / ui-ux / marketer are **hints for PM**, not auto-launch rules.
- **Minimum for behavior-change** (unless PM narrowed otherwise): after user OK, the eng roles from cast + `qa` write/verify. BA / architect / ui-ux / marketer / security / devops / tech-writer run only if PM included them.
- If **security** is in cast: its open blocker holds close. If not in cast: close does not wait for security.
- If **tech-writer** is in cast: close after its handoff. If not: do not invoke.

## Roster

| Invoke | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `/orchestrator` | Parent: execute PM cast only; Task briefs; closeout + retro |
| `/business-analyst` | Market scan, compare approaches, grill, `product.md`, journeys |
| `/architect` | Cross-layer design; `architecture.md`; constraints for PM |
| `/pm` | Scope, `agent.md`, **role cast**, ask «можно начинать?» |
| `/ui-ux` | Flows, UI contract, a11y; assimilate marketer sellability tips |
| `/marketer` | Copy + UI-for-sellability tips in docs; not locale JSON / not React |
| `/backend-dev` | `apps/api`, workers, DB, webhooks; `packages/**` when owner |
| `/frontend-dev` | `apps/dashboard` + dashboard locale JSON; `packages/**` when owner |
| `/qa` | Two phases: write failing tests before eng; verify after |
| `/security` | Threat review; `security.md`; must-fix; no signature-skip |
| `/devops` | Infra, env docs, deploy wiring |
| `/tech-writer` | CODEMAP / reports / runbooks / eng docs sync |

## Pipeline (max template; PM selects subset)

Ordered **template** — roles absent from cast are simply skipped:

1. **BA** → grill as needed → `product.md` / journeys
2. **architect** (if in cast) → `architecture.md` + constraints for PM
3. **PM** → `agent.md` + **role cast** + parent epic + **AC child issues** → **stop for user OK**
4. Optional parallel after product intent (if in cast): **ui-ux** ∥ **marketer**
5. After «ок / делай»: **qa** with `phase: write` — failing tests from acceptance (`docs-before-code` / red)
6. **backend-dev** ∥ **frontend-dev** (non-overlapping trees; API contract in `agent.md`) — make QA tests green; do not weaken or delete them
7. **security** (if in cast) — after eng; before or with verify; blockers hold close
8. **qa** with `phase: verify` — re-run tests, AC matrix, report gaps; close passed AC issues
9. **devops** (if in cast) — infra/env
10. **tech-writer** (if in cast) — docs sync near closeout
11. Roles coordinate via **handoff comments on the parent issue** (no role-stage tickets). **Close the parent GitHub issue** when the feature stage is done: after **qa verify** succeeds, if devops/tech-writer were **not** in cast (or already done), **qa** (or orchestrator) **closes** parent with `gh issue close N`. If devops or tech-writer ran, close parent after their handoff (that role or orchestrator).
12. Orchestrator merges results, updates specs/memory if scope changed, writes stage report when handing off «готово», posts **closeout retro**; confirms AC children closed or tracked and no open role-stage leftovers

Task prompts for QA **must** include `phase: write` or `phase: verify`.

### Bug fast-path

Only inside an active `/dev-team` run (or as **single-agent** work with no team). Clear repro: PM/orchestrator may publish a **short cast** without BA/PM/ui-ux/marketer (typical: `qa write → owner eng → qa verify`; add security/tech-writer only if in cast). Lint/format/commit-only: no full team. Do **not** invent a fast-path cast via `Task(orchestrator)` when the user never typed `/dev-team`.

## Shared ownership

One working tree. Enforce ownership in prompts and `agent.md`:

| Zone | Owner rule |
| --- | --- |
| `apps/api`, workers, DB, webhooks | `backend-dev` only |
| `apps/dashboard` | `frontend-dev` only |
| `packages/**` | **Not** parallel with FE/BE. Owner in `agent.md` (default `backend-dev`; `frontend-dev` only if PM explicitly said dashboard-facing) |
| Cabinet i18n locale JSON | **`frontend-dev` only**. Marketer writes copy proposals in `docs/specs/<slug>/` (`copy.md` / `marketing.md`) |
| Landing | Marketer; content in the landing repo only when that repo is in the workspace **and** Task explicitly allows |
| Planning roles (BA/PM/architect/ui-ux/marketer/tech-writer) | **docs/** (+ agreed content) only — policy B |

Marketer ↔ ui-ux: marketer proposes sellability layout tips in docs; ui-ux folds them into the UX contract. **ui-ux veto** only for a11y / design-system conflicts. Disputes on “how to sell” → user/PM.

If two implementers must touch the same files, run **sequentially** or serialize via orchestrator.

## Acceptance IDs (AC-N)

- BA numbers product acceptance in `product.md` as `AC-1`, `AC-2`, …
- PM mirrors/refines done-criteria in `agent.md` with the same `AC-N` IDs (add eng-only ACs if needed; do not renumber silently)
- **qa write:** every new/changed test maps to one or more `AC-N`
- **qa verify:** handoff includes matrix `AC-N → pass | fail | gap`; close AC child issues that pass
- Eng/security must-fix should cite `AC-N` when fixing acceptance gaps

## Handoff-meta

Every role `gh issue comment` handoff **must** end with:

```markdown
### handoff-meta
- slug: …
- issue: #N
- stage_issue: #AC… | n/a | #N
- role: …
- status: done|blocked
- paths: …
- commands: …
- ac_covered: AC-1, …
- follow_ups: #A, #B   # tech-debt / future issues; omit if none
- next: …
```

- `issue:` is always the **parent epic**.
- `stage_issue:` may list the **AC child issue(s)** currently worked, the parent `#N`, or `n/a` / omit when N/A. **Never** invent a separate role/phase GitHub issue for this field.
- Omit `commands` / `ac_covered` only when truly N/A (e.g. pure planning with no tests yet); still keep the other fields.

## Stuck escalation (2-cycle)

After **2** eng↔qa fix→verify cycles **without a new signal** (new failing test insight, new AC clarification, or new repro): post `## blocker · <role> — <slug>`, stop spinning, escalate to user/PM. Do not burn CI/token budget on the same failure.

## Closeout retro

On stage close / «готово», orchestrator posts a short issue comment with **3 bullets**: what broke in (1) handoff, (2) ownership, (3) AC tracing — or «нет» per item. Use `memory_lesson_save` / rule tweak **only** if the pattern repeats across tickets.

## GitHub ticket (required) — LOCKED policy

Non-trivial team work uses **parent epic + AC child issues only**. Roles do **not** get their own GitHub issues.

1. **Parent epic (required):** **PM** (or orchestrator if PM skipped) ensures a **parent** issue exists — `gh issue create --assignee @me` if missing; put `#N` / URL into `product.md` / `agent.md`.
2. **AC child issues (required for numbered acceptance):** after AC list is known, PM/orchestrator creates **one GitHub issue per `AC-N`** (title preferably starts with `AC-N …`). Body links parent `#N`. Put the map `AC-N → #M` into `agent.md`. **qa verify** (or eng when agreed) closes AC issues that pass.
3. **Do NOT create role/stage issues.** Forbidden titles / pattern: `[<slug>] · <role-or-phase>` (e.g. `qa write`, `backend-dev`, `frontend-dev`, `qa verify`, `ui-ux`, `pm`, …). Do **not** `gh issue create` for cast stages. Roles run via **cast + handoff comments on the parent**.
4. Every delegated Task prompt **must** include `issue: #N` (parent). Optionally include `stage_issue:` as AC ticket(s) being worked, parent `#N`, or omit / `n/a`.
5. **Every role that runs** ends by posting a handoff comment on the **parent** issue via `gh issue comment N`. No silent handoff. Include **handoff-meta** (`stage_issue` = AC / parent / n/a — never a role-stage issue).
6. Roles do **not** close a “stage issue” for their role — there is none. Close **AC** children when that acceptance passes (typically qa verify).
7. **Blockers and clarifications** also go on the **parent** ticket — not only in chat or memory. Post them as soon as they appear (do not wait for role end).
8. Orchestrator may add a final summary + **closeout retro** when closing the stage / «готово».
9. **Who closes the parent issue:** after acceptance is met — **qa** (verify phase) when devops/tech-writer are skipped; otherwise after those cast roles’ handoffs (**devops** / **tech-writer** / **orchestrator**). Prefer AC children closed (or explicitly deferred as follow-ups) before closing parent. Never leave a done parent ticket open solely because a skipped role was not scheduled.

If a stray `[<slug>] · <role>` issue appears: close it as **not planned** with a short note that role-stage tickets are discontinued; keep AC tickets.

### What must be commented

| Kind | When | Heading prefix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Handoff | End of role work | `## <role> — <slug>` (QA: `## qa write` / `## qa verify`) |
| Blocker | Work cannot proceed (missing API, env, decision, access) | `## blocker · <role> — <slug>` |
| Clarification | Need user/PM/other-role answer to continue correctly | `## уточнение · <role> — <slug>` |
| Closeout retro | Orchestrator at stage end | `## closeout retro — <slug>` |

Chat may mirror the same text; the **issue thread is canonical**. If a blocker/clarification is resolved, post a short follow-up comment (`## resolved · …`) with the decision.

### Handoff template

```bash
gh issue comment N --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## <role> — <slug>

**Сделано:** …
**Пути:** …
**Блокеры / вопросы:** … (или «нет»; если есть — отдельный comment уже должен быть)
**Следующему:** …

### handoff-meta
- slug: …
- issue: #N
- stage_issue: #AC… | n/a | #N
- role: …
- status: done|blocked
- paths: …
- commands: …
- ac_covered: …
- follow_ups: …
- next: …

EOF
)"
```

### AC child issue template

```bash
gh issue create --assignee @me --title "AC-N …" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
Parent: #N
AC: AC-N
Done when: acceptance met; qa verify (or owner) closes this issue after PASS.

EOF
)"
```

### Blocker / clarification template

```bash
gh issue comment N --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## blocker · <role> — <slug>
# or: ## уточнение · <role> — <slug>

**Суть:** …
**Почему блокирует / зачем ответ:** …
**Нужно от:** user | pm | business-analyst | architect | backend-dev | …
**Предлагаемые варианты:** … (если есть)

EOF
)"
```

Roles: `orchestrator`, `business-analyst`, `architect`, `pm`, `ui-ux`, `marketer`, `backend-dev`, `frontend-dev`, `qa`, `security`, `devops`, `tech-writer`.

## Tech debt → follow-up issues (no silent debt)

See also `no-tech-debt.mdc`.

- Do **not** accumulate unpaid tech debt in code (`TODO`/`FIXME`/skipped tests/temporary hacks) without a filed issue.
- Deferred / out-of-scope cleanup discovered mid-flight → **new GitHub issue** (label `tech-debt` when useful), linked from the role handoff. Do **not** expand the current cast into unbounded cleanup.
- Work still required for current `AC-N` stays in the current parent ticket — file a follow-up only for true future work.
- Orchestrator/PM may batch tiny related debt into one follow-up issue; still must be a real issue, not chat-only.

## Delegation

- Put full context in the Task prompt (slug, **issue #N** parent, optional **stage_issue** = AC ticket(s) / parent / omit, paths, **AC-***, ownership, constraints, depth S/M/L; for QA also **`phase: write|verify`**; for security optional **`phase: review|fix`**). Subagents do not see this chat. Remind roles to file follow-up issues instead of silent tech debt — **do not** create or close role-stage issues.
- Launch independent roles in **one** message (parallel Task calls) **only** when the cast marks `∥`.
- Resume a subagent for follow-ups when continuity helps.
- Subagents inherit MCP including **agentmemory** — expect recall at start and `team-handoff` save at end.
- After each role: confirm the issue comment was posted (URL or comment id in the role return).

## agentmemory

- After `agent.md`: `memory_save` agent spec — concepts `agent-spec`, `<slug>` (PM/orchestrator)
- BA: brief `product-intent` / `journey` — do not dump full `product.md`
- Each role: `team-handoff` + role concept (`backend`, `frontend`, `ui-ux`, `qa`, `infra`, `marketing`, `architecture`, `security`, `docs`, …)
- Include `issue:#N` in handoff content when known

## Anti-patterns

- Assembling the multi-role team without an explicit `/dev-team` in the user message (soft «собери команду» / «команда» does not count)
- Calling `Task(subagent_type: "orchestrator")` on ordinary feature/bug asks («сделай X», «Enter confirms delete», UI polish) — **forbidden**; do the work as a single agent or wait for `/dev-team`
- Treating «chat once ran orchestrator» as a standing license for every later request
- Launching roles outside the PM role cast (or without updating cast after user override)
- Starting FE/BE before user OK on a non-trivial feature
- Starting FE/BE before **qa write** on a non-trivial behavior change (unless user explicitly skips)
- Parallel FE+BE without a written API/UI contract
- Parallel FE/BE edits to the same `packages/**` tree
- Marketer editing dashboard locale JSON or React
- Using marketer/ui-ux to bypass product grill
- Orchestrator re-implementing everything instead of delegating large role-shaped chunks
- Finishing a role without an issue comment / without **handoff-meta** when `issue: #N` was provided
- Leaving blockers or clarifications only in chat/memory without an issue comment
- Eng weakening/skipping QA tests to go green; verify phase skipped after FE/BE
- Spinning more than 2 fix→verify cycles without a new signal
- Leaving the GitHub issue open after qa verify PASS when later cast roles were skipped
- Creating role/stage GitHub issues (`[<slug>] · <role-or-phase>`) — **forbidden**; use parent + AC children only
- Shipping silent tech debt (TODO/FIXME/skipped tests) without a follow-up GitHub issue
